                  "file_path": "result.txt",
                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_02\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit renames the test file's package/directory from `com.github.piotr.rusin.yule` to `com.github.piotr_rusin.yule` so that it matches the main application's actual package. The commit message states this was fixing \"a test initialization error\" because \"No application configuration could be found\" \u2014 a classic Spring Boot `@SpringBootTest` failure that occurs when the test class's package does not match (or is not a parent of) the package containing the `@SpringBootApplication` class, since Spring Boot's context loader searches upward from the test's package to find the application configuration.\n\nTracing the history:\n- candidate_01 is the initial project scaffold. Here both the main class (`YuleApplication.java`) and the test class (`YuleApplicationTests.java`) live under the same package/directory: `com.github.piotr.rusin.yule`. At this point everything is consistent \u2014 no bug exists yet.\n- candidate_02 renames/moves the main source files (`YuleApplication.java`, `Post.java`) to the corrected package `com.github.piotr_rusin.yule` (matching the pom.xml groupId `com.github.piotr-rusin.yule`), but it does NOT update the test file, which remains at `src/test/java/com/github/piotr/rusin/yule/YuleApplicationTests.java` with the old package declaration `com.github.piotr.rusin.yule`. This is precisely the moment the main and test packages diverge, causing the `@SpringBootTest` context to fail to locate the application configuration \u2014 exactly the bug described in the fix commit message.\n- candidate_03 is identical to the fix commit itself (it performs the rename of the test file to `com.github.piotr_rusin.yule`), so it is the fix, not the cause.\n\nTherefore candidate_02 is the commit that introduced the mismatch between the main and test packages, which is the root cause fixed later.\n"
